(7616028, 1232616, 138630, '<td valign="top">I love the depth here and the undulating terrain with the hills laid in over one another like stairs that go out rather than up or down.  I am not sure what that little thing in the sky just above the horizon in the center is, but I wish it was either not there or clearly recognizable as something of interest. Voted earlier.</td>', 'I love the depth here and the undulating terrain with the hills laid in over one another like stairs that go out rather than up or down.  I am not sure what that little thing in the sky just above the horizon in the center is, but I wish it was either not there or clearly recognizable as something of interest. Voted earlier.', '2019-02-28 16:05:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(7616029, 1233036, 138630, '<td valign="top">Absolutely fantastic moment with both parents there, the worm in the mouth, and four wide-open beaks!  While I do a lot of painterly work myself and usually quite enjoy it, this is one time that I would have liked a more "photographic" look.  Maybe you didn''t have good focus on everyone, though - truly just getting the capture is fantastic.  Voted earlier but I think I''ll bump.</td>', 'Absolutely fantastic moment with both parents there, the worm in the mouth, and four wide-open beaks!  While I do a lot of painterly work myself and usually quite enjoy it, this is one time that I would have liked a more "photographic" look.  Maybe you didn''t have good focus on everyone, though - truly just getting the capture is fantastic.  Voted earlier but I think I''ll bump.', '2019-02-28 16:07:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(7616032, 1232673, 138630, '<td valign="top">A beautiful girl, great focus and tones.  I''m having trouble with the pose - whose arms are these, anyway?  Clearly the forward arm is hers, and I guess the other is, too . . .   but there''s something very strange about the very straight edge of her forearm. I like the spots of sunlight though the one on the bridge of her nose is distracting.  Can''t get away from those eyes, though . . . so it''s an 8 from me.  Voted earlier.</td>', 'A beautiful girl, great focus and tones.  I''m having trouble with the pose - whose arms are these, anyway?  Clearly the forward arm is hers, and I guess the other is, too . . .   but there''s something very strange about the very straight edge of her forearm. I like the spots of sunlight though the one on the bridge of her nose is distracting.  Can''t get away from those eyes, though . . . so it''s an 8 from me.  Voted earlier.', '2019-02-28 16:13:49.000000', NULL, 1),
